  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The points \\(A(-3,y_1)\\), \\(B(1,y_2)\\), and \\(C(2,y_3)\\) all lie on the parabola \\(y=-x^2\\). What is the order of \\(y_1\\), \\(y_2\\), and \\(y_3\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y_1>y_2>y_3\\)",
    "B": "\\(y_3>y_2>y_1\\)",
    "C": "\\(y_2>y_1>y_3\\)",
    "D": "\\(y_2>y_3>y_1\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Substituting each value gives \\(y_1=-9\\), \\(y_2=-1\\), and \\(y_3=-4\\), so \\(y_2>y_3>y_1\\). This can also be determined from the fact that the parabola opens downward and the function value decreases as the distance from the axis of symmetry increases.",
